course: dictionary
lesson: 7463
title: Populous: lots of people
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Populous is an adjective. It describes a place that has a lot of people living in it. «Nigeria is Africa's most populous country, with about 230 million people» tells you that many people live there.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. The sentence gives a huge number of people, so populous must mean having many people. Try the swap: «Nigeria is Africa's most full of people living in it country» is clumsy, but the meaning fits, so you know you are right.
explain: Populous is about how many people live somewhere, not how big the place is. A large country with few people is not populous. Look for the phrases: «a populous city», «the most populous country».
fact: Populous means having a lot of people living in it.
fact: Populous is an adjective, so it describes a place: «a populous city».
fact: «India and China are the two most populous countries, each with about 1.4 billion people.»
fact: «India overtook China around 2023», so India became the most populous country then.
fact: Populated is a close word that is more common in everyday speech: «a densely populated area» means many people live close together.
exercise: «Nigeria is Africa's most populous country, with about 230 million people.» What does populous mean here? | *Having a lot of people living in it | Very far away from other places | Having lots of trees and parks | Very cold for most of the year
exercise: «India and China are the two most populous countries.» Find and copy the word that tells you about the number of people. | countries | two | *populous | India
exercise: In maths, «the most populous» means the one with what? | *The biggest number of people | The smallest number of people | The highest mountain | The oldest buildings
test: What does «a populous city» mean? | A city with lots of parks and gardens | A city that was built long ago | *A city with a lot of people living in it | A small village by the sea
test: Which place would be described as populous? | A dry desert with no houses | A lake with no boats on it | A quiet, empty island | *A busy city full of people
exam: Which sentence uses populous correctly? | The populous mountain was very tall and covered in snow | *The most populous country has the most people living in it | The populous river flowed slowly through the fields | The populous forest was quiet at night
